1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,760
Let's look at the build system of Android.

2
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:05,580
Android uses a build system named soon.

3
00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:12,720
You might have also heard that Android also uses the build systems like Make Katie and Ninja.

4
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:17,640
Let's see what role these all systems play in building Android.

5
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:25,290
The Android Build System uses Android blueprint files and Android make files to build the Android OS.

6
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:32,220
As you might have already noticed, there are two types of build files that are BP blueprint files and

7
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:34,710
standard emmc make build files.

8
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:38,700
Why should Android use two types of build files?

9
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:46,380
Historically, before Android seven Android use the make build system to build Android.

10
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,050
So that means.

11
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:52,500
Earlier it was only using download files before Android seven.

12
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:59,850
So the problem was that the build was pretty slow, error prone and scalable and it was also difficult

13
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,560
to test for the developers.

14
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:04,860
So Google decided to improve the build system.

15
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:09,820
So then Google decided to use the new build system named soon.

16
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:15,330
Sony is basically the replacement of the old Android make build system.

17
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:21,210
It replaces Android MK files with the Android dot BP files.

18
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:25,440
So Android P files are similar to the JSON syntax.

19
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:28,980
The Aosp theme is still converting the make files.

20
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:34,990
So these make files into the BP files, but it's not yet completed.

21
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:39,360
That's why there are still many make files in the system.

22
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:45,390
All the standard files will be gradually cleaned up in one of the future versions of Android.

23
00:01:45,390 --> 00:01:46,610
So that is the reason.

24
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:50,910
Basically we are seeing two types of files for building the system.

25
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:58,550
So the Android or BP files are there to stay and Android files will be replaced in future.

26
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:06,690
The new song Build System passes through the BP files or the blueprint files and outputs a ninja build

27
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:07,080
file.

28
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:15,720
Zoom also uses a tool named Katie to convert the make files into ninja files, and these ninja files

29
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:19,230
are an input to the ninja build system.

30
00:02:19,230 --> 00:02:26,010
Under the build folder we could find make build system and the so built system there are many other

31
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:27,600
supporting packages as well.

32
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:35,820
The make build system or the Katie Build system is basically a clone of the original make build system,

33
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:39,540
so you can find more information about the build system in the read me here.

34
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:47,340
And the basic purpose of Katie is to convert the make files, the DOT MK files into the Ninja files

35
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,740
and the new songbird system.

36
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:56,940
So this is basically written in programming language and the song build system basically converts the

37
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:00,710
standard BP files into the ninja files.

38
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:09,030
As we understood so far, the DOT BP files and the make files are getting converted into the ninja format.

39
00:03:09,030 --> 00:03:16,680
The simple system converts the BP files into ninja files and the Katie build system converts the make

40
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,960
files into the ninja files.

41
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:27,390
So at the end there is ninja build file and these ninja build files are the input to the ninja build

42
00:03:27,390 --> 00:03:27,900
system.

43
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:31,500
You can find all these ninja files under the out folder.

44
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:36,360
So out folder is where we have all the build intermediate files.

45
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:39,590
So here you can find the ninja files.

46
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:45,600
This is generated by Katie and this is how a ninja build file looks like.

47
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:49,410
And this is the input to the ninja build system.

48
00:03:49,410 --> 00:03:58,350
This ninja built file is then passed by the Ninja Build System to build the required Android OS files.

49
00:03:58,350 --> 00:04:06,330
So these include compiled shared objects, the standard so files, Java archives, the starter jar files

50
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:10,200
apps, the standard APK files and the executables.

51
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:18,510
So at the end, the Ninja build system converts all these ninja build input files into the Android OS

52
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,350
files.

